IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 6, Service of documents (ss 28A, 29).
-- Section 29 (when service by post is taken to be effected) is in
-- au-interpretation-time.l4, because it fixes a DAY. This module has s 28A: which methods
-- of serving a document an Act that requires or permits service allows.
-- Sections 24 to 28 and 30 to 32 are repealed (endnote 4).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.

§ `Part 6: Service of documents`

§§ `Section 28A: methods of service`

DECLARE `Kind of person served` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Method of service` IS ONE OF
    `delivering it to the person personally`
    `leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document`
    `sending it by pre-paid post to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document`
    `leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate`
    `sending it by pre-paid post to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate`
    `any other method`

-- 28A(1) says the document "may be served" by the listed methods; 28A(2) says nothing in
-- (1) takes away another law of the Commonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that
-- authorises another method, or a court's power to authorise another method. Whether such
-- a law or court order exists for the method in hand is an INPUT.
-- src:610 | 28A Service of documents
-- src:611 | (1) For the purposes of any Act that requires or permits a document to be served on a person, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send” or any other expression is used, then the document may be served:
-- src:612 | (a) on a natural person:
-- src:613 | (i) by delivering it to the person personally; or
-- src:614 | (ii) by leaving it at, or by sending it by pre-paid post to, the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document; or
-- src:615 | (b) on a body corporate—by leaving it at, or sending it by pre-paid post to, the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate.
-- src:616 | Note: The Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information in writing by means of an electronic communication.
-- src:617 | (2) Nothing in subsection (1):
-- src:618 | (a) affects the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth, or any law of a State or Territory, that authorises the service of a document otherwise than as provided in that subsection; or
-- src:619 | (b) affects the power of a court to authorise service of a document otherwise than as provided in that subsection.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 28A (src:610-619)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person served`
      method IS A `Method of service`
      `another law or a court authorises that method` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`service by this method is permitted` kind method `another law or a court authorises that method` MEANS
    IF `another law or a court authorises that method`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a natural person` THEN
             CONSIDER method
             WHEN `delivering it to the person personally` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `sending it by pre-paid post to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN JUST TRUE
             -- s 28A(1) says a document "may be served" on a natural person by the methods in paragraph (a); it does not say that a natural person may not be served at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of a body corporate.
             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
             WHEN `leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN NOTHING
             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
             WHEN `sending it by pre-paid post to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN NOTHING
             -- s 28A(1) lists the methods by which a document "may be served"; it does not say that no other method is permitted, and s 28A(2) says that nothing in subsection (1) affects another law or a court's power that authorises service "otherwise than as provided in that subsection".
             -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
             WHEN `any other method` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
             CONSIDER method
             -- s 28A(1) says a document "may be served" on a body corporate by the methods in paragraph (b); it does not say that a body corporate may not be served by the methods listed for a natural person.
             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
             WHEN `delivering it to the person personally` THEN NOTHING
             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
             WHEN `leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN NOTHING
             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
             WHEN `sending it by pre-paid post to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN NOTHING
             WHEN `leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `sending it by pre-paid post to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
             -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
             WHEN `any other method` THEN NOTHING
